## How work is tracked across chats
Each chat is a separate session, but they all share these files as memory. To start a new
chat with full context: read this file, then `logbook/HANDOFF.md`.

Two layers of memory:
- **`run_log.md`** — the dated timeline (what happened, in order, chronological).
- **`logbook/NN_*.md`** — one file per work-stream (deep context: goals, decisions, files,
  next steps). Use these for "how / why did we do X."

Rule of thumb: work happens in a module → update that module file + add a dated line to
`run_log.md`. If the immediate next action changes, overwrite `logbook/HANDOFF.md`.

